{"type":"WebSearch","query":"California Proposition 37 election results November 3 2026","content":"**California Proposition 37 (the Second Mortgage Homebuyer Program and Revenue Bond Initiative) is on the November 3, 2026, general election ballot as an initiated state statute.** It would authorize the California Housing Finance Agency (CalHFA) to issue up to $25 billion in revenue bonds to fund a new “middle-class homeownership loan” program. Eligible buyers (California residents for at least one year, with household income at or below 200% of area median income, occupying the home as a primary residence) could receive a fixed-rate second mortgage covering up to 17% of the purchase price of a qualifying new home (or first sale of converted non-residential property), while putting down at least 3% themselves. Bonds would be repaid by homeowners’ loan payments, with no direct cost to taxpayers. Homes would be subject to county-based price caps (generally around $1 million–$1.5 million). A “yes” vote supports creating the program; a “no” vote opposes it.[[1]](https://ballotpedia.org/California_Proposition_37,_Second_Mortgage_Homebuyer_Program_and_Revenue_Bond_Initiative_(2026))

**Unofficial election results are not yet available.** As of the latest official data (November 2, 2026, evening), 0% of precincts are reporting, with 0 votes counted for Yes or No. Polls close at 8 p.m. PT on November 3. Results will be updated live on the California Secretary of State’s election night site after that time, with certification expected by December 11, 2026. Vote-by-mail, provisional, and other ballots will continue to be counted afterward.[[2]](https://electionresults.sos.ca.gov/returns/ballot-measures/county)

Pre-election polling (e.g., PPIC) showed support around 61–65% Yes. Live tracking is available via the Secretary of State, CNN, and other outlets. For the full voter guide, see the official California Voter Information Guide.","citations":["https://ballotpedia.org/California_Proposition_37,_Second_Mortgage_Homebuyer_Program_and_Revenue_Bond_Initiative_(2026)","https://electionresults.sos.ca.gov/returns/ballot-measures/county"],"allowed_domains":null}
